WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Crankshaft and rods. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Trace piston force through a slider-crank

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: The connecting rod links piston travel to crank rotation. Its angle changes through the cycle, so forces and leverage change too.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: Sketch crank center, crank pin, rod and piston pin as four linked points before predicting motion.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Annotated force diagram

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Ideal mechanism only; friction, heat and part-specific behavior need measurements.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Trace piston force through a slider-crank
